{
  "spec": "priest-discipline",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Discipline priest healer rotation (stage 2 of the healer build), written against the fork's fake raid: the healer is raid player 0, the four fake party members are players 1 to 4 and the tank is player 5. Reference build: 33 points in Discipline and 18 in Holy (engine talent string 005203031305101531-0350500302: Twin Disciplines 5, Silent Resolve 2, Improved Power Word: Shield 3, Mental Agility 3, Inner Focus, Meditation 3, Mental Strength 5, Soul Warding, Penance, Renewed Hope 5, Divine Aegis 3, Power Infusion; Improved Renew 3, Holy Specialization 5, Divine Fury 5, Inspiration 3, Improved Healing 2). Penance is cast on its cooldown at whoever is hurt, the tank is shielded when he is hurt and Weakened Soul is off, and the filler is the efficient Heal rank 4 (the top rank of Heal, which the site's rank rewrite leaves alone). Power Infusion is only used when the player names a target for it; the major-cooldown pass casts it. Renew is left out on purpose: against the fork's test profile it returned less health per mana than Penance and Heal. Mana pacing: the filler, Prayer of Healing and Power Word: Shield fire at their normal thresholds only while the mana bar is at least 90% of the share of the fight left (currentManaPercent against remainingTimePercent); behind that pace the filler waits for a tank under 50% and a member under 35% and the shield waits. Penance and the emergency Flash Heals are never paced. On the site's heal profile at raid gear this lifted effective HPS about 12% and the time before the mana bar empties about 80% against the unpaced list; the rest of the 300 s is the profile asking more than one mana bar holds.",
